{
  "server_url": "https://your-server.com",
  "nickname": "테스트-장치-01",
  "package_name": "com.example.app",
  "check_interval_seconds": 3
}

/*
 * MapleTing Python Client Configuration
 * ======================================
 *
 * Copy this file to config.json and edit with your values.
 * 
 * Configuration Fields:
 * ---------------------
 * 
 * server_url (string, required):
 *   The URL of the Next.js server that receives heartbeats.
 *   - Development: http://localhost:3000
 *   - Production: https://your-deployed-server.com
 *   - Must be a valid URL with protocol (http:// or https://)
 *   - Do NOT include trailing slash
 * 
 * nickname (string, required):
 *   Display name for this monitored device/application.
 *   - Can be in any language (UTF-8 encoded)
 *   - Examples: "테스트-장치-01", "テスト-デバイス", "测试设备", "Device-01"
 *   - Treated as opaque text (not used as database identifier)
 *   - Nickname will be auto-created on first heartbeat if it doesn't exist
 *   - Multiple devices can report under the same nickname
 *
 * package_name (string, required):
 *   Android package name of the app to monitor.
 *   - Found via: adb shell pm list packages
 *   - Examples:
 *     - MapleStory M: "com.nexon.ma"
 *     - YouTube: "com.google.android.youtube"
 *     - Chrome: "com.android.chrome"
 *   - Must be a valid Android package name (reverse domain notation)
 * 
 * check_interval_seconds (number, optional):
 *   How often to check if the app is running (in seconds).
 *   - Default: 3 seconds
 *   - Recommended range: 3-10 seconds
 *   - Lower values = faster detection but higher CPU/battery usage
 *   - Higher values = slower detection but lower resource usage
 *   - Minimum: 1 second
 *   - Maximum: 60 seconds
 * 
 * 
 * Example Configurations:
 * -----------------------
 * 
 * Korean Device:
 * {
 *   "server_url": "https://mapleting.example.com",
 *   "nickname": "메이플-서버-01",
 *   "package_name": "com.nexon.ma",
 *   "check_interval_seconds": 3
 * }
 *
 * Japanese Device:
 * {
 *   "server_url": "https://mapleting.example.com",
 *   "nickname": "テスト-サーバー-01",
 *   "package_name": "com.example.app",
 *   "check_interval_seconds": 5
 * }
 *
 * English Device (Development):
 * {
 *   "server_url": "http://localhost:3000",
 *   "nickname": "Test-Device-01",
 *   "package_name": "com.example.testapp",
 *   "check_interval_seconds": 3
 * }
 * 
 * 
 * Finding Your Package Name:
 * ---------------------------
 * 
 * 1. Install the app on your Android device
 * 2. Enable USB debugging
 * 3. Connect device via ADB
 * 4. List all packages:
 *    adb shell pm list packages
 * 5. Search for your app:
 *    adb shell pm list packages | grep keyword
 * 
 * Common package names:
 * - MapleStory M: com.nexon.ma
 * - MapleStory Worlds: com.nexon.msw
 * - YouTube: com.google.android.youtube
 * - Chrome: com.android.chrome
 * - Netflix: com.netflix.mediaclient
 * - Spotify: com.spotify.music
 *
 *
 * Testing Your Configuration:
 * ----------------------------
 * 
 * 1. Verify ADB connection:
 *    adb devices
 * 
 * 2. Verify app is running:
 *    adb shell ps | grep your-package-name
 * 
 * 3. Test the monitor:
 *    python monitor.py
 * 
 * Expected output:
 *   🔍 Monitoring started for: 테스트-장치-01 (com.example.app)
 *   📱 Check interval: 3 seconds
 *   Press Ctrl+C to stop
 *   Initial status: RUNNING
 * 
 * 4. Test heartbeat to server:
 *    curl -X POST https://your-server.com/api/heartbeat \
 *      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
 *      -d '{"nickname":"your-nickname","status":"connected","timestamp":1234567890000}'
 * 
 * 
 * Troubleshooting:
 * ----------------
 * 
 * Problem: "config.json not found"
 * Solution: Copy this file to config.json in the same directory as monitor.py
 * 
 * Problem: "Invalid JSON in config.json"
 * Solution: Validate JSON at https://jsonlint.com/
 *   - Check for trailing commas (not allowed in JSON)
 *   - Ensure all strings use double quotes (not single quotes)
 *   - Verify all brackets are closed
 * 
 * Problem: "Missing required config keys"
 * Solution: Ensure all required fields are present:
 *   - server_url
 *   - nickname
 *   - package_name
 *
 * Note: Nicknames are auto-created on first heartbeat if they don't exist
 *
 * Problem: "Rate limited" when sending heartbeat
 * Solution: Wait at least 55 seconds between heartbeats for the same nickname
 * 
 * Problem: App not detected as running
 * Solution: 
 *   - Verify package name is correct
 *   - Check if app is actually running: adb shell ps | grep package-name
 *   - Some apps use different process names
 *   - Try launching the app first, then start monitor
 * 
 * 
 * Security Best Practices:
 * ------------------------
 *
 * 1. Never commit config.json to version control
 * 2. Use HTTPS in production (not HTTP)
 * 3. Keep config.json permissions restricted (chmod 600 on Unix)
 * 4. Be aware that any device can send heartbeats for any nickname
 * 5. Rate limiting prevents spam (55 seconds per nickname)
 * 
 * 
 * Support:
 * --------
 * 
 * For issues or questions:
 * - Server documentation: ../server/README.md
 * - API reference: ../server/API.md
 * - Deployment guide: ../DEPLOYMENT.md
 * 
 * 
 * Version: 1.0.0
 * Last Updated: 2025-12-23
 */
